    {
      "type": "content",
      "id": "art-show",
      "label": "Nobody Came To My Art Show.",
      "classes": "sortable",
      "aria": "Nobody Came To My Art Show",
      "chapter": null,
      "body": [
        {
          "kind": "beat",
          "id": "show-canvas",
          "layout": "beat flip",
          "heading": "Nobody Came<br>To My Art Show",
          "heading_tag": "h2",
          "heading_class": "big r",
          "role": "EXHIBITION + PERFORMANCE ART",
          "fact": "The exhibition began before anyone entered. As performance art, I ran through Hollywood in a clown costume carrying a pink-wrapped canvas marked <b>“nobody came to my art show.”</b> Invitations arrived as pieces of concrete marked “break.” On opening night, a 2,000-pound concrete monolith blocked the gate with the painting buried inside. The crowd had to break it open to enter.",
